    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule: the owner response now includes `bulkSignupWarning: true` when more than 80 owners already share the owner's (business-day-adjusted) registration day, and `false` otherwise.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (with getter/setter).\n\n2. **`.../function/owner/BulkSignup.java`** (new) \u2014 A small helper that counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals the effective business day and returns `count > 80`. It reuses the existing `BusinessDay.effective(...)` logic, so it shares the same day-accumulation path as the daily-limit rule (`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`, which caps the same day at 100).\n\n3. **`.../function/owner/RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder) and **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder) \u2014 Both now inject `OwnerRepository`, compute the flag via `BulkSignup.warning(...)`, and set it on the DTO before responding.\n\nNotes on design choices:\n- The warning is computed at response time in the responder steps (which already run under a transaction) rather than in the MapStruct mapper, since it needs the repository \u2014 the mapper only has the entity.\n- The count keys off the owner's own registration day, matching the existing daily-limit accumulation semantics, so a GET and the originating POST report the same value for a given day.\n- The `Cp22Tests` acceptance test and all 32 other tests pass.",
